{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And I am amazed</b> at the commentary of the associate of Ephraim, who said that ויתמהמה is from the root מה, but he forgot that the two hehs are with mappiq; rather it is a word of delay, its root is quadriliteral, and the pe is doubled." "<b>And they seized hold.</b> He explains that he was afraid and had no strength to flee,"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Reading חבר בן אפרים literally as 'the associate of Ephraim,' following the voice rule of minimal resolution; the phrase may refer to a specific Karaite interpreter. Ibn Ezra says the root is 'quadriliterate' (משולש) though this term more commonly means 'triliterate'; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:09.629071547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}